        "objects": ["b-mast", "b-knob", "b-beam", "b-pivot", "b-left-sling-outer", "b-left-sling-inner", "b-right-sling-inner", "b-right-sling-outer", "b-left-pan", "b-right-pan", "b-base", "b-left-foot", "b-right-foot"],
        "assertions": ["b-beam-level", "b-equal-arms", "b-pan-level", "b-mast-perpendicular"]
      },
      {
        "id": "b-source-cylinder-pair",
        "description": "Left pan has one short squat cylinder (roughly x=644..727, y=258..301); right pan has one tall narrower-looking cylinder (roughly x=839..885, y=171..293). Elliptical top rims and curved lower edges make both cylinders recognizable. The source's perspective widths and outlines are schematic, not calibrated. There are no material labels, numbers or units on these source cylinders. Complete edition prose identifies lead and aluminum, says their masses are equal, and gives aluminum volume as almost 4 times lead volume. Assign lead left and aluminum right. No numerical cylinder mass is supplied and none is invented.",
        "objects": ["b-lead-body", "b-lead-top", "b-aluminum-body", "b-aluminum-top", "b-lead-material", "b-aluminum-material"],
        "assertions": ["b-equal-cylinder-diameters", "b-lead-height", "b-aluminum-height", "b-cylinder-common-baseline"]
      },
      {
        "id": "b-source-subfigure-mark",
        "description": "The source has one Cyrillic b-shaped subfigure mark below the balance (around x=772..795, y=338..367). Modern equivalent is Latin (b), included in an English heading. No additional source caption is inside this crop.",
        "objects": ["b-heading"],
        "assertions": []
      },
      {
        "id": "modern-edition-data-and-scale",
        "description": "Modern additions, NOT source-pixel labels: English Ice/Iron/Lead/Aluminum names; (a)/(b) equal-mass headings; each block's 1 t mass and ice 1.1 m^3 / iron 0.13 m^3 volumes from complete s12 prose. t means metric tonne, not US short ton. Block-front edges are regularized to 122.26468351149 and 60, with the same oblique projection; their implied 3-D volume ratio is (122.26468351149/60)^3 = 1.1/0.13 = 8.461538..., preserving both printed numbers and the prose's approximate eightfold comparison. Cylinder radii are regularized equal, heights 40 and 160, so the illustrated comparison is the prose's approximate fourfold volume relation, not a new density measurement. The extra displayed V(Al) ~ 4 V(Pb) is sourced from prose. The hydrogen example has no object in source fig-48 and no hydrogen container is added. Subfigures are stacked for mobile; neutral semantic fills replace old hatching and engraving.",
        "objects": ["a-ice-material", "a-ice-mass", "a-ice-volume", "a-iron-material", "a-iron-mass", "a-iron-volume", "b-volume-relation"],
        "assertions": ["a-ice-front-width", "a-ice-front-height", "a-iron-front-width", "a-iron-front-height", "b-equal-cylinder-diameters", "b-lead-height", "b-aluminum-height"]
      }
